cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this code, the descriptor registries or the released results, please cite both the article and this deposit.
title: "Compact Vision-Language Models for Cross-Crop Plant-Disease Diagnosis at the Edge: A CPU-Only Study - code, descriptor registries and results"
abstract: >-
  Code, descriptor registries and result files for a study of what lets a small, frozen
  vision-language model diagnose crops it was never trained on. Seven ways of authoring the
  class descriptions are compared across nested held-out sets of 16, 34 and 51 unseen classes on
  four compact contrastive encoders, alongside a CPU latency and INT8 benchmark. The deposit
  reproduces every number and figure in the article from the released result files; the images
  themselves are the SAGE crop-disease dataset at revision bc9bd2899f and are not redistributed
  here.
